		<summary type="html">&lt;div class=&quot;K2FeedIntroText&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;lyrics&lt;/strong&gt; from the DEMO of &lt;strong&gt;&quot;Give Me All Your Love,&quot;&lt;/strong&gt; the lead single (co-produced with Martin Solveig) from &lt;strong&gt;Madonna's new album&lt;/strong&gt;, have been revealed by our friends at &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.madonnarama.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; title=&quot;Madonnarama&quot;&gt;Madonnarama.com&lt;/a&gt;. Keep in mind that the demo did not include Nicki Minaj neither M.I.A. This demo is already circulating among &lt;strong&gt;Madonna&lt;/strong&gt;'s collectionists.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The site also point out that &lt;strong&gt;&quot;Give Me All Your Love&quot;&lt;/strong&gt; is &quot;one of the fun, radio friendly tracks and  absolutely perfect for the Super Bowl,&quot; but &quot;the overall album contains much  more deeper and personal lyrics,&quot; as we also reported.&lt;/p&gt;
